Features:
Dynamic Command-Line Args to specify model 
Model weights and biases stored in 1D array
activation func method: accounts if simple activation func that is able to be undone, if not, we use caching to store previous z value.

# adjust
we only cache for activation funcs that destroy the gradients (so we can't use the current activation as an cheap computational substitution) and/or are too computationally expensive to undo to retrieve the z value?

Forward pass: implemented with recursion to go thru deeper each layer, and for loop for iterating thru each individual node in layer

Backward pass: implmented with recursion to propagate thru layers until reach very first hidden layer, used dC/db to calculate dC/dw instead of recalculating C'a(z(w)) * a'(z(w)) since: 
Change of Cost to biases: C = cost (aka loss), a = activ, z = value before activation b = bias
dC/db = C'(a(z(w))) * a'(z(w)) * 1
dC/db = C'(a(z(w))) * a'(z(w))
Change of Cost to Weights: C = cost (aka loss), a = activ, z = value before activation w = weight 
dC/dw = C'(a(z(w))) * a'(z(w)) * z'(w)
dC/dw = C'(a(z(w))) * a'(z(w)) * a(prev)
dC/dw = dC/db * a(prev)

